    "report_markdown": "# Late Shipment Analysis – GERMANY Suppliers (1992–1998)\n\n**Overall late rate: 63%**\n\n## Key Drivers (Supported)\n| Factor | Bucket | Late Rate | Gap vs Best |\n|--------|--------|-----------|-------------|\n| **Promised window (order → committed)** | 30–50 d | 79.3% | +32.6 pp |\n| | 71–90 d | 46.7% | baseline |\n| **Transit time (ship → receipt)** | 21–30 d | 71.1% | +16.4 pp |\n| | 01–10 d | 54.7% | baseline |\n\n## Ruled Out (No Meaningful Difference)\n- **Ship mode**: 0.7 pp spread (e.g., AIR 62.9%, FOB 62.5%)\n- **Order priority**: 0.9 pp spread (e.g., 3-MEDIUM 62.5%, 4-NOT SPECIFIED 63.4%)\n- **Shipping instruction**: 1.3 pp spread (e.g., TAKE BACK RETURN 62%, COLLECT COD 63.3%)\n\n## Inconclusive\n- **Supplier nation/region**: Too little data (smallest bucket n=51465).\n\n## Recommended Actions\n1. Extend promised window commitments to align with the 71–90 d band.\n2. Reduce transit time towards the 01–10 d band.\n3. Enforce a dispatch lag under 31 d to mitigate the 50.3% late rate seen in the 31–60 d bucket."
